{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"fdfe8a2e3e819db4","type":"group","x":-273,"y":-779,"width":1602,"height":1006,"label":"Potion of Youth"},
		{"id":"0f13eabacbf1fd50","type":"text","text":"Sara laughed. \n\n\"Nothing about this is funny.\"\n\n<!-- She hackled louder, \"Oh this takes me back.\" Her voice went dark, \"Ug, I haven't felt this in so many years.\" she turned to Vald, \"Come at me you bastard, that all you fucking got?\" -->\n\nShe hackled louder, \"Oh this takes me back.\" Her voice went dark, \"It's been so many years.\" she turned to Vald, \"That all you fucking got? Come at me for real, you bastard!\" Sara didn't hold back when it came to sparring with Lilith or Don, but this wasn't a sparring match. This was a street fight, where there were no rules. Meaning she could push herself harder than she had since she was human. ","x":-240,"y":-220,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"90ccee2e2e6cf890","type":"text","text":"Don supposed Sara as they came near the house. \"The sitter sees this, and she's going to flip.\" \n\n\"I'll got ahead and send her home, it'll only tkae a moment.\"\n\nDon and Lilith lead Sara to an out of sight spot, and waited.\n\n\"Ok, she's gone.\" Jane said from the porch. \"Anne and Savanna are asleep.\"\n\nThey came near the stairs, when Sara stopped, \"Hold on, we're still in dark form.\"\n\n\"Right.\" Don said. \n\nIt took each of them a slightly different amount of time to focus, but they are changed back to their normal appearance before heading into the house.\n\nBut, unbeknownst to them, Savanna has been watching from her window. Half asleep, she scurried back to her bed. This had to be some bazar dream. ","x":860,"y":-220,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"268cf2805712c311","type":"text","text":"\"While your manner of speech is rather crude, even for modern standards, I must admit a certain respect for the brutality you fight with. You may have been turned, but I recognize you as a true vampire.\" Vlad tilted his head slightly at Sara, then waved at an underling. \n\n\"Hank you.\" Her busted mouth made her the words sound slightly off. It was hard to read her expression through the damage to her face, but Vlad could read her body language: she held it close, treasuring and guarding it.\n\n\"If I may ask, for what do you seek the (whatever) for?\"\n\nSara looked to Lilith, who nodded, \"We can trust him.\" \n\n\"To trade with (name). We're going to make ambrosia.\" \n\n\"The food of the Gods. So, what lucky member of the departed is it for?\" \n\n\"My child.\" \n\nVlad nodded, \"A noble cause, to be sure.\" Then he waved to dismiss them.","x":220,"y":-220,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"90d7d7321d7eb978","type":"text","text":"I'm thinking whatever Sara is fight Vlad for, it's one a unique item. Like there's only 1 or 5 in the world type object. Sometimes he can get more of. Some of his blood, something from an animal he has, something from a cave on his land, something renewable. Where he can get more of it. ","x":-40,"y":-740,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"79b919082d3d0bbd","type":"text","text":"Lilith is going meet Alexander Goth at the university where Caleb needs either something to help him translate part of something for Emma or like he needs to talk to a professor or something. \n\nFor some reason related to helping Emma, they're at the university. In a coffee shop or a library or something like that, and Alex happens to be there dressed down to blend in. Lilith doesn't know he's a Goth when they meet, and she doesn't care even when she finds out. \n\n","x":-40,"y":-1680,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"033a79b2fa1459fa","x":360,"y":-1680,"width":400,"height":400,"type":"text","text":"\"How clever, a witty remark for sure.\" Lilith clicked her tongue. This human was rather smug. If only he knew. But there was no affinity for the darkness in this one, so finding out would end poorly for him. \n\n\"Then I apologize for offending a lady. What noble family do you hail from?\" "},
		{"id":"d32feb2a9e648511","type":"text","text":"\"How did it go with Miss Ruhesh?\" Lilith asked. Last time they'd met Alex had said he was to meet another young lady, per his parents' attempts to find him a wife. \n\n\"She seemed... nice, I suppose.\" He frowned. \n\nLilith raised an eyebrow, \"And that is an issue?\" \n\n\"So many of them do, because all they are interested in is my family's name or wealth. Or both.\" He sighed. \n\nAh, Lilith supposed that made sense: for human women to generally act interested in Alex, but not for who he was as a person. Rather because they sought what a marriage to him would mean for themselves. \"Well, is there a method you've used to tell their true interests?\"\n\n\"The only method I've found is to give it time. At least most people show their true colors eventually. A crack in the mask, even if only brief.\" Alex tisked. \"I must admit, the routine of waiting for that to happen... is getting tiring.\" \n\n\"Do you even want a wife?\" She asked, but not because she wanted the answer, to get him to ask himself. \n\nHe scoffed. \"It's easier to deal with selfish young women than it was trying to deal with my parents when I refused to meet them.\" He rubbed his eyes, \"No, that is not the proper way to say it. They care for me, they truly do.\" He paused, \"Perhaps there are no words that correctly fit it.\" \n\nLilith nodded, \"There are things that are not words for.\" she reached her arms around him. ","x":1100,"y":-1680,"width":400,"height":400},
		{"id":"52240931542db5de","type":"text","text":"\"Sometimes I wish this wasn't temporary.\"\n\n\"Trust me, you do not want me for a wife.\"\n\n","x":1500,"y":-1680,"width":400,"height":400}
	],
	"edges":[]
}